  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Let the maximum elongation of the spring be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0069_94e2f68c601b.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 215px;\" /></p><p>Using energy conservation</p><p>Loss in kinetic energy of both blocks<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo></math>Gain in spring energy</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>k</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p></blockquote>"
